  "description": "NASFIY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C66 H86 Dy4 Mn2 N12 O22,4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 22 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.298-3.843 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.32-130.29°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C66H86Dy4Mn2N12O22·4(C2H3N). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III), Dy(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
